Package: spatialcluster
Title: Spatially Contiguous Clustering with the 'Redcap' Algorithm
Version: 0.2.1.007
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Mark", "Padgham", , "mark.padgham@email.com", role = c("aut", "cre")), 
      person("Michael", "Sumner", role = c("ctb"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2471-7511")))
Description: Groups spatial data into clusters of similar observations, while
    requiring that each cluster forms a single spatially contiguous region.
    Contiguity is enforced by first building a spanning tree from the spatial
    relationships between points, and then cutting that tree into clusters
    according to a matrix of distances or other measures of similarity. Trees
    may be built from first-order relationships only (direct neighbours),
    yielding a minimum spanning tree, or from full-order relationships between
    entire clusters, using single linkage (nearest members), average linkage
    (mean of all pairs), or complete linkage (furthest members). The single and
    average linkage methods implement the 'Redcap' algorithm ('Regionalization'
    with dynamically constrained agglomerative clustering and partitioning).
    Results can be visualised as maps of clusters, cluster hulls, or trees.
